<<~ ahu slot=`#/inscription`>>
! Exact typography

```tiddlywiki
<<art worktype=`minimal typographic poster` subject=`a short instruction to notice the present moment` read=`a quiet invitation, not an advertisement` imagery=`one large line of lettering above ample visual rest` treatment=`warm restrained ink impression with subtle letterpress-like edge character` composition=`one asymmetrically balanced line with generous margins` relation=`the text and unprinted space establish a deliberate pause` depiction-scope=`only the poster; no maker, photographed office, or metadata labels`>>
```
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/verification`>>
!! Check

Inspect the actual letters, punctuation and hierarchy after export; a visually plausible generated inscription is not a verified string.

Exact source text belongs in a separately checkable artifact contract.

```toml
[artifact]
exact_text = "NOTICE THE PRESENT."
spelling_and_punctuation = "mandatory"
validation = "inspect final letters or typeset deterministically"
```

<<~/ahu>>

